{"parentUuid":"5d805911-465a-4ede-92bc-e6b96092a191","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cb157cbc-04b8-42a8-b4f9-93a7625ecfc4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XoCGCBY9xozGsrGEkLRxdS","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"T17\",\n  \"title\": \"Closing task: update track-f-resolution-extraction.json's AC-F6 to the new call-site text\",\n  \"files\": {\n    \"modify\": [\n      \".claude/specs/track-f-resolution-extraction.json\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"Add a failing shell-level check (no Rust test needed -- this is a JSON text edit). From /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto, run:\\n```\\npython3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nd = json.load(open('.claude/specs/track-f-resolution-extraction.json'))\\nac = next(a for a in d['acceptance_criteria'] if a['id'] == 'AC-F6')\\nassert 'resolve_package_config(&id, &cfg_with_local_promotions)?' in ac['criterion'], 'new text missing'\\nassert 'resolve_package_config(&id, cfg);' not in ac['criterion'], 'stale binding text (a) still present'\\nassert 'replaced by a single call to resolve_package_config(&id, cfg).' not in ac['criterion'], 'stale prose text (b) still present'\\nprint('OK')\\n\\\"\\n```\",\n    \"Expected failure: `AssertionError: new text missing` -- AC-F6's current `criterion` field still reads the pre-Result call-site text ending in `let pkg_override = resolve_package_config(&id, cfg);`, which also still contains BOTH stale substrings that must be removed by the fix below: (a) the exact stale binding `resolve_package_config(&id, cfg);` and (b) the stale prose fragment `replaced by a single call to resolve_package_config(&id, cfg).`.\",\n    \"Use a non-destructive raw-text replace, not a JSON parse-mutate-dump round-trip (which would reflow unrelated formatting in the file). In Python:\\n```python\\nimport json\\npath = '.claude/specs/track-f-resolution-extraction.json'\\nraw = open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8').read()\\nd = json.loads(raw)\\nac = next(a for a in d['acceptance_criteria'] if a['id'] == 'AC-F6')\\nold_text = ac['criterion']\\nnew_text = (\\n    'The inline two-pass [[package]] lookup in walk.rs (lines 160-169, the two '\\n    'cfg.packages.iter().find(...) calls joined by .or_else, followed by '\\n    '.map(|(_, cfg)| cfg)) is removed and replaced by a single call to '\\n    'resolve_package_config(&id, &cfg_with_local_promotions)?. The trailing '\\n    '.map(|(_, cfg)| cfg) at line 169 is deleted because resolve_package_config '\\n    'already returns Result<Option<&PackageConfig>, GraphError>, not '\\n    'Option<&(PackageId, PackageConfig)>. The resulting binding is: let '\\n    'pkg_override = resolve_package_config(&id, &cfg_with_local_promotions)?;, '\\n    'where cfg_with_local_promotions is the build-local ResolvedConfig overlay '\\n    'constructed via cfg.with_promoted_siblings(...) per '\\n    'SPEC-TRACK3B1-IDENTITY-PROMOTION-CORE. All tests in '\\n    'crates/callisto-graph/tests/per_package_config_test.rs pass without modification.'\\n)\\nold_escaped = json.dumps(old_text)[1:-1]\\nnew_escaped = json.dumps(new_text)[1:-1]\\nassert raw.count(old_escaped) == 1, f'expected exactly one occurrence of the old escaped criterion text, found {raw.count(old_escaped)}'\\nraw2 = raw.replace(old_escaped, new_escaped, 1)\\nopen(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8').","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a6ade5c5-5013-4a03-8bfa-989246aac942","timestamp":"2026-08-17T13:03:10.872Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\n  \"id\": \"T17\",\n  \"title\": \"Closing task: update track-f-resolution-extraction.json's AC-F6 to the new call-site text\",\n  \"files\": {\n    \"modify\": [\n      \".claude/specs/track-f-resolution-extraction.json\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"Add a failing shell-level check (no Rust test needed -- this is a JSON text edit). From /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto, run:\\n```\\npython3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nd = json.load(open('.claude/specs/track-f-resolution-extraction.json'))\\nac = next(a for a in d['acceptance_criteria'] if a['id'] == 'AC-F6')\\nassert 'resolve_package_config(&id, &cfg_with_local_promotions)?' in ac['criterion'], 'new text missing'\\nassert 'resolve_package_config(&id, cfg);' not in ac['criterion'], 'stale binding text (a) still present'\\nassert 'replaced by a single call to resolve_package_config(&id, cfg).' not in ac['criterion'], 'stale prose text (b) still present'\\nprint('OK')\\n\\\"\\n```\",\n    \"Expected failure: `AssertionError: new text missing` -- AC-F6's current `criterion` field still reads the pre-Result call-site text ending in `let pkg_override = resolve_package_config(&id, cfg);`, which also still contains BOTH stale substrings that must be removed by the fix below: (a) the exact stale binding `resolve_package_config(&id, cfg);` and (b) the stale prose fragment `replaced by a single call to resolve_package_config(&id, cfg).`.\",\n    \"Use a non-destructive raw-text replace, not a JSON parse-mutate-dump round-trip (which would reflow unrelated formatting in the file). In Python:\\n```python\\nimport json\\npath = '.claude/specs/track-f-resolution-extraction.json'\\nraw = open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8').read()\\nd = json.loads(raw)\\nac = next(a for a in d['acceptance_criteria'] if a['id'] == 'AC-F6')\\nold_text = ac['criterion']\\nnew_text = (\\n    'The inline two-pass [[package]] lookup in walk.rs (lines 160-169, the two '\\n    'cfg.packages.iter().find(...) calls joined by .or_else, followed by '\\n    '.map(|(_, cfg)| cfg)) is removed and replaced by a single call to '\\n    'resolve_package_config(&id, &cfg_with_local_promotions)?. The trailing '\\n    '.map(|(_, cfg)| cfg) at line 169 is deleted because resolve_package_config '\\n    'already returns Result<Option<&PackageConfig>, GraphError>, not '\\n    'Option<&(PackageId, PackageConfig)>. The resulting binding is: let '\\n    'pkg_override = resolve_package_config(&id, &cfg_with_local_promotions)?;, '\\n    'where cfg_with_local_promotions is the build-local ResolvedConfig overlay '\\n    'constructed via cfg.with_promoted_siblings(...) per '\\n    'SPEC-TRACK3B1-IDENTITY-PROMOTION-CORE. All tests in '\\n    'crates/callisto-graph/tests/per_package_config_test.rs pass without modification.'\\n)\\nold_escaped = json.dumps(old_text)[1:-1]\\nnew_escaped = json.dumps(new_text)[1:-1]\\nassert raw.count(old_escaped) == 1, f'expected exactly one occurrence of the old escaped criterion text, found {raw.count(old_escaped)}'\\nraw2 = raw.replace(old_escaped, new_escaped, 1)\\nopen(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8').","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5d805911-465a-4ede-92bc-e6b96092a191","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
