{"parentUuid":"183bf43a-07fb-4bb3-ae55-e8ff3d2268fc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8Pb1smf7g7UbJKa9xem","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have a clear picture now. Here's the state of things:\n\n**Track 3a (workspace-membership filtering) — complete.** All 45 tasks landed (I did TASK-01–32 this session with a mid-session `lambda-reviewer` pass that approved cleanly; agy finished TASK-33–36). Every criterion in the 34-criterion spec has a dedicated regression test, most were adversarially verified non-vacuous by temporarily breaking the logic and confirming the test catches it.\n\n**Track 3b1 (identity promotion core) — functionally complete, one task uncommitted.** All of T01a–T16 are committed and match the plan. T17 (the closing task — updating `track-f-resolution-extraction.json`'s AC-F6 to the new `resolve_package_config` call-site text) is done correctly but sitting **uncommitted** in your working tree. I verified it against the plan's own check script — it passes. There's also an uncommitted, unrelated small cleanup in `ecosystem_bugs_test.rs` (a `find`+`.expect()` pattern replaced with `any`+`assert!`) that I can't attribute to any specific task — it's harmless and the test still passes, but it's undocumented.\n\n**Track 2 (platform-manifest/optionalDependencies writes) — a real process gap.** The master remediation plan explicitly called this a full-pipeline track requiring a canon spec, flagging it as needing careful integration with Spec A/B's write-batching data-loss-prevention invariants (`classify_manifest_writes`). Instead it landed as a single direct commit (`2d53001`) — no spec file exists, no plan, just 81 lines in `apply.rs` with one happy-path test. I traced through the execution order: the new `platform_writes`/`optional_dep_updates` loops run sequentially *after* the batched-write classification completes, so it's not unsafe today, but it bypasses the batching invariant entirely (double I/O if a path is touched by both paths) and has none of the malformed-input/error-case coverage the rest of this codebase's tracks get.\n\n`just ci` passes fully right now (all 7 phases, exit 0). `ACTIVE.md` hasn't been updated for any of this — it still ends at the post-Track-G audit entry."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2041,"cache_read_input_tokens":305362,"output_tokens":3737,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2603},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2041,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3737,"cache_read_input_tokens":305362,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2041,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2041},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8PavNdQVsXvhFNpA8FU","type":"assistant","uuid":"91375cdf-b48f-484f-910a-7380cdc384e9","timestamp":"2026-08-17T13:21:59.782Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
