{"parentUuid":"506abced-3fb2-4253-a503-72b8da4f9c1e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8SqvExPTmdWZuxpZDuR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The audit confirms the stale-handle-clobber concern was **not real** — sequential execution with always-fresh disk reads makes the two dispatch loops safe today. But it surfaced something more important: **`plan.platform_writes`/`plan.optional_dep_updates` are never populated anywhere in production** — every real plan-producer (`version.rs`, `snapshot.rs`, `pr_body.rs`) hardcodes them empty. Agy wired up the *consumption* side (the dispatch loops) but the actual planning logic the master plan called \"design and build from scratch\" was never built — Track 2 is maybe a fifth done. The consumption code that does exist has two genuine but currently-dormant bugs:\n\n- **Lockfile staging blind spot**: `active_ecosystems` (which drives lockfile refresh/staging) is derived only from `plan.bumps`, never from `platform_writes`/`optional_dep_updates` — so once real data flows through, a `pnpm-lock.yaml` etc. would silently go stale.\n- **No precondition check**: unlike every sibling write loop (which verifies `current == expected` before writing), the `platform_writes` loop unconditionally overwrites — a hand-edited or already-bumped file gets silently clobbered instead of erroring.\n\nBoth are inert only because nothing reaches them yet."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5288,"cache_read_input_tokens":317457,"output_tokens":1724,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":863},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5288,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1724,"cache_read_input_tokens":317457,"cache_cr